              "summary": "**Evaluating design constraints**\n\nIn powered scenes, a model toy may be painted, but if it’s legally drawn, it could be powered down, allowing us to remove the glow requirement while keeping the turbine design. The visor doesn't need to be glowing all the time either. I wonder if removing these elements counts as “changing content.” There's some ambiguity around legal constraints about merging or stripping content. The coloring also confuses things—legal drawings are monochrome, yet face paint colors suggest some color rendering is expected.**Clarifying constraints and merging**\n\nI need to retain the canonical colors and avoid using the \"Gipsy Danger logo/34\" since it's not provided. It's puzzling whether all original constraints should be removed or just duplicates merged. When we remove something, it should be unique items or clauses that don't apply anymore. So for the record, we might include aspects like giant scale, but I'll consider if wheel/tracks are redundant. The first step states to deduplicate, but maybe removed entries should just be noted rather than discarded.",
